### TODO list confirmation

- Do not unilaterally generate or commit a TODO list. Always present it as a proposal and request the user's confirmation first.
- When proposing a TODO list:
  - Structure items clearly with short titles and one-line rationale.
  - Include estimated scope/impact and any risks or prerequisites per item.
  - Group by priority or dependency when relevant.
- Do not persist TODOs in code comments, tasks, or external trackers without explicit approval.
- Keep TODO items actionable (clear owner and tentative timeline) once approved; otherwise, avoid leaving TODO markers in code. See `docstrings-style.mdc`.
- Follow `wait-for-review.mdc` (pause after proposal), `complex-edits-confirm.mdc` (plan before complex work), and `edit-explanation.mdc` (include concise rationale with approved changes).
